(a) In accordance with O.C.G.A. § 38-3-56, before building, constructing, repairing, renovating or making improvements to any real property, including dwellings, homes, buildings, structures or fixtures within an area in the unincorporated area of the county designated in a declared emergency or disaster, any person, firm, partnership, corporation or other entity must register with the county development board and secure a building permit that is posted at the worksite. Each day any such entity does business in the county without complying with this article constitutes a separate offense.
(b) The cost of registration fees in a declared emergency or disaster shall be fixed by action of the board from time to time and set out in the consolidated fee schedule. Registration is nontransferable. The cost of the emergency building permit shall be equal to the cost for a building permit under existing regulations. The permit shall only be authorized for repairs.
